findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified that from_file_or_default swallows all errors. The
    config loading tests and reviewer findings don't mention this specific issue of
    treating parse/permission errors the same as NotFound.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer F10 flags that ConfigError Display leaks raw config content\
    \ verbatim, contradicting the security doc comment. TEA also wrote CWE-209 tests.\
    \ However, the core issue of eprintln leaking CliError Display to stderr is only\
    \ partially caught \u2014 reviewer noted ConfigError leaks but verified ServerError\
    \ suppresses details."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: "TEA wrote CWE-113 header injection tests for CR/LF in tenant ID and auth\
    \ token. Dev implemented with_tenant stripping CR/LF (client.rs:45). Reviewer\
    \ verified header injection prevention. However, the deeper issue \u2014 using\
    \ raw String instead of TenantId from axiathon-core \u2014 was not flagged by\
    \ any phase."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged that dependencies use direct version strings instead
    of workspace = true. The reviewer noted a toml version mismatch (F5) but not the
    workspace inheritance pattern violation across all 6 deps.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer F7 explicitly flags: ''RawConfig silently ignores unknown fields
    including token... A warning should be emitted, or unknown fields should be explicitly
    handled.'' TEA also wrote config_ignores_token_field_in_file test but the test
    only verified token() returns None, not that a warning is emitted.'
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: "Reviewer stated 'Tests are thorough and non-vacuous \u2014 assertions\
    \ check specific values, not just is_ok()' under VERIFIED items. The vacuously\
    \ true assertion pattern (is_none() || ...) was not identified by any phase."
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Reviewer verified tests as non-vacuous but missed the specific test with
    zero assertions (let _ = config). No phase flagged a test that only checks non-panic
    without any assert statements.
